The airport you're looking for is **Telluride Regional Airport** (ref W315390123) in Telluride, Colorado.

It sits in a narrow slot canyon in the San Juan Mountains of the Rocky Mountains, and its short runway is perched on a ridge with a steep drop-off at the end — a "cliff-edge" approach that travelers frequently compare to the famous, treacherous landings at Paro Airport in Bhutan. According to [My Travelling Circus](w1), Telluride is the one US landing experience that rivaled Paro, where you "literally land on the top of a cliff in the middle of the Rocky Mountains."

