The Methodist Church in Bodie State Park (on Fuller Street, Bodie, California) was built in **1882**. It is Bodie's only church that still stands — a Catholic church was also built in Bodie in 1882, but it burned in a 1928 fire.

According to [Flying Dawn Marie](w1), the church is one of the first notable features on a self-guided tour of the park, and [California Travel / Amateur Traveler](w3) confirms Bodie got its first church, the Methodist Church, in 1882.

