The Chi Lin Nunnery (志蓮淨苑) in Diamond Hill, Kowloon, Hong Kong was originally established in **1934**, founded as a retreat for Buddhist nuns.

The complex you see today is a later reconstruction: it was rebuilt in the 1990s in Tang Dynasty style (entirely of wood, without nails) and reopened in 1998, according to [Wikipedia](w6) and [Becky Exploring](w2).

