The historic building right next to Bright Angel Lodge is the **Buckey O'Neill Cabin** — a small log cabin on the Rim Trail, about 100 m (a short walk) northwest of the lodge. It's a National Historic Landmark, built in 1905 by prospector "Buckey" O'Neill, who was the first person to descend the Grand Canyon on a bicycle.

A couple of other historic spots are also nearby if you want to wander: the **El Tovar Hotel** (a 1905 Harvey House hotel) is about 270 m to the east, and the **Bright Angel Trailhead** viewpoint is roughly 290 m to the west.

